  landscapes but the coupling protocol between them.

  A coupling protocol is a structure that:
  1. Is constituted by agents — no agents, no protocol (Monk E is right that
  agents are always present)
  2. Has causal power over agents — it channels, constrains, and selects among
  agent behaviors (Monk D is right that this power is irreducible to individual
