  specifications, organizational hierarchies, social norms, protocol standards.
  These are the structures through which convergent power-seeking dynamics
  propagate. They are not agents (they don't have goals). They are not
  landscapes (they don't exist independently of agents). They are the interface 
  layer that translates between individual agent behavior and system-level
  dynamics.

